  "statement": "Let $x=2^{1/3}+2^{-1/3}$. Show that $x^{3}-3x=\\tfrac52$.",
  "solution": "$x^{3}=(2^{1/3})^{3}+3(2^{1/3})^{2}(2^{-1/3})+3(2^{1/3})(2^{-1/3})^{2}+(2^{-1/3})^{3}=2+3\\cdot2^{1/3}+3\\cdot2^{-1/3}+\\tfrac12=\\tfrac52+3x$. Hence $x^{3}-3x=\\tfrac52$.",
